so it's been three days since the m2  macbook pro came out and we have done a  ton of tests and comparisons and put out  multiple videos in this one i want to  give you guys a short video about the  good the bad and the outright ugly about  this laptop and my perspective for real  world use with this laptop instead of  just benchmarks now the first thing for  a positive that i want to talk about is  the webcam now a lot of people have  really hated on apple for sticking with  the 720p webcam and i agree they should  have put a 1080p in but it does look  better now the weird thing is is that  it's only better because of software  they tweaked the algorithm for the noise  reduction they added better contrast or  else that's what it looks like now with  that the 14 inch and 16 inch and even  the upcoming m2 macbook air are still  going to look more detailed sharper less  noise  but at least they've done the software  fix which they should do to the previous  ones to make it look a little bit better  now the second thing that i noticed is  the speakers now in my comparison  against the m1 macbook pro i said that  they sound about the same i couldn't  hear much of a difference but then some  of you guys called it out and said that  no in fact the m1 has better dynamics it  sounds better and the truth is when we  were listening i told him that i thought  that the bass was better on the m1 and  it sounded slightly louder it just  didn't make sense why that would happen  and because i was unsure i was just  leaving it up to you guys but you guys  spoke and with that when we monitored in  final cut it did show about a two  decibels louder kind of volume on the m1  model so i don't know why the m2 doesn't  sound as good the m1 already was the  worst sounding macbook out of the full  lineup so that is definitely unfortunate  now the next thing is the fan  now this thing when you're using it day  to day  it almost seems like a macbook air that  is fanless  you don't hear it unless you're doing  heavy rendering for a very long time and  i'm not talking about running a couple  runs of cinebench it still is silent  apple let this thing heat up the most we  recorded is 104 on screen but actually  hit 105  and they didn't care the fans only  barely started to ram up ramp up there  so they're treating it more like a  macbook air instead of a pro whereas the  m1 pro even though it uses less power  and less wattage and has less heat the  fans actually ramp up quicker now that  is a positive if you don't want to hear  the fans day to day if you have a  previous intel model and you're annoyed  of it well this is going to be way  better it's a great experience not  hearing that fan but for those of you  guys that are concerned about the high  heat  that the chip gets and how hot it gets  well you could download tg fan pro and  you can change the settings yourself to  have it spin up a little bit earlier  yeah you don't have to make it be crazy  loud but at least spin up if it's  hitting 100 degrees now one thing i  really wish this thing had was fast  charging we've been testing these things  running down the batteries and it takes  forever to charge it up closer to three  hours whereas the rest of the lineup now  as far as charging 50  in just 30 minutes and so that when you  do have to charge that is an  inconvenience but flipping over to the  battery life it is  incredible for light uses  better than the m1 macbook pro which is  already amazing now dave lee actually  did some very in-depth testing he has  this chart so i'm not going to make my  own i'll show you his thank you dave and  this thing for light uses is shockingly  good and it works really good because it  has the larger more powerful efficiency  cores that apple updated so it doesn't  have to use the performance cores as  much but on the flip side if you are  going to start pushing it that is when  the battery life does get worse than it  was before because it is using roughly  33 percent more power in order to gain  about 13 more performance on the cpu and  then the graphics also uses more power  as well and of course we already  mentioned ssds in multiple videos we  made a video specifically about that  performance  and this is just something that is very  sad that this is happening now i know  apple needs to make money maybe there's  not enough chip supply and so they're  trying to do a single chip instead of  two but it's just weird having a product  that came out a year and a half later  that is an expensive product with the  pro name on it but the ssd is half the  speed compared to before now we already  mentioned that what i didn't mention is  slc caching now when you're transferring  a large file most of these ssds  they will actually slow down after a  certain amount is written and what i  found is that with the  256 gig model on the m2 it actually  slows down earlier so about 40 45 gigs  and then it slows down from about 1 300  megabytes per second  all the way down to about an average of  200 250 now the m1 also the base model  256 gig it will actually record right at  uh 1900 from my external ssd and it also  does slow down takes a little bit longer  but then when it slows down it's still  riding over 400 so i actually  transferred a big file which is our test  folder with a bunch of different  benchmarks the m2 took 5 minutes and 34  seconds while the m1 took 2 minutes and  55 seconds and keep in mind it actually  would have been quite a bit faster if we  had a faster external ssd this one is  just our favorite because it's universal  it's a great price  so that is unfortunate because not only  will it slow down even more with the soc  cash but also if you guys didn't see our  ssd test video with real world tests  when you're opening up professional  applications a bunch of tabs it is less  responsive than the macbook and i wanted  to do that test just to see  um  was i right was this actually less  snappy and in fact it is and  professional uses also slow down if  you're loading up the same amount of  tabs and applications on the m1 versus  m2 the m2 gets slower which is insane  and that just brings me to you know my  kind of thoughts on this machine it  should not be called pro in 2022  now if this came out at the time that m1  did it still have been a great update  compared to the intel model but we're  taking one step back the ssds can't keep  up with most of these thunderbolt drives  now the whole system slows down if you  open up multiple applications  so if you do want to have a laptop for  light simple tasks you're going to get  insane battery life  it's going to work well  but that means it's not a pro machine so  that is just the weird thing about it  now we're gonna do some more testing  we're gonna look at video editing um  some more in-depth stuff so make sure  you guys are gonna watch that if you  guys want more info  but for your guys's questions people are  asking should i jump to the 16 gig model  or 512 because we're now not  recommending the base model because the  ssds are slow and the whole system slows  down  well it depends on how much uh space you  need for example if you don't use more  than 256 gig like i do jump up to 16 gig  if you want to have more space well then  that speed is gonna kick back up to the  level of the m1 at the base even though  you have to spend 200 bucks more and  that makes it a much more responsive  system when you're using it so i would  uh i would end up  getting more storage if you feel like  you might need it but if not kick up the  ram and then the hard thing is if you  kick both up well at that point you're  not far off from the 14 inch which is  our next comparison and you can buy one  of those for 200 bucks off right now on  amazon so 100 bucks more than the m2  that is crazy i will link that down  below now about the m2 macbook air  they're asking will the m2 macbook air  ssds  we will see i sure hope not but i think  if apple is doing this to their pro  machine i would expect the m2 macbook  air to also get slower  compared to the previous generation and  the last question we're getting is  should you just buy an m1 refurbished or  used or a discount compared to getting  the m2 model well if you're getting a  good price on it i think yes especially  if you want to get the base model  because  you are going to have a snappy system  when you open up a bunch of tabs or  programs it's still going to stay  quicker than if you would have had an m2  at that base configuration  and even though the cpu is faster on the  m2 it's not a huge difference you're  still going to be very happy with the m1  and then if you don't use the graphics  you're not constantly pushing it that  part will matter to you at all so if  you're getting a nice discount and of  course amazon has great deals they're  clearing these out now i think you'll be  happy with it or the m1 macbook air  which was our favorite laptop or until  the m21 comes out so there you guys go  if you have any other questions you want  us to cover in our full review after  we've done more testing go ahead and ask  down below click above to subscribe  check out one of those great videos  right over there that's been max and  i'll see you in the next video  [Music]

